at are looking to replace  them with potential franchise  quarterbacks and then you have the teams  that just have crappy quarterbacks or no  quarterbacks and they're going to be  looking for quarterbacks as well and I  know we started this process with teams  speaking very poorly about this class  and it's not very good and this that the  other thing as we get closer and closer  they got the over/under in Vegas at  three and a half and I think it's going  to go for and there's an outside chance  it goes five the  because where else are you going to find  potential franchise quarterbacks they're  not available typically in free agency  and if they are there's usually a reason  for it like a serious injury so you got  to hope you can find a guy that you can  groom and you have the luxury if you've  got Drew Brees Philip Rivers Ben  Roethlisberger Eli Manning as the  starter for the next year or two  putting that guy on the bench and  letting him learn and it worked out  pretty well for Aaron Rodgers three  years on the bench in Green Bay behind  Brett Farr but you also want them in the  first round as well because you get to  lock them up a year longer than if they  go after that yeah that fifth year  option is a huge bonus but you know the  other thing to that anchor of being a  first-round pick that pressure the  expectation that's why it's almost  better for teams at the bottom that had  quarterbacks to say I'm not going to be  compelled to put the guy on the field I  do get him for five years he learns from  a veteran now some of these veterans may  not be thrilled  Carson Palmer more than willing to  mentor a young quarterback but what's  Ben Roethlisberger going to say we  already know what Drew Brees is going to  say he said it why you going to use a  first-round pick on a quarterback when  I'm still here and I think we're going  to have another layer of drama that  emerges if some of these teams that that  know the clock is ticking very loudly on  their current quarterback decides to use  a first-round pick on another one he's  Mike Florio from pro football TOCOM if  you were going to look at the  quarterback most likely to be a bust  you know I've interviewed each of the  top six and I like all of them now I  can't comment on how their game is going  to translate from the college level the  pro level we know there's a ceiling at  some point between what they've done in  college and what they're under whether  they get to the end of the Pro Football  Hall of Fame there's a ceiling there and  it's a crapshoot at the 50/50  proposition you know I look at Mitchell  true Biscay and I say this guy's got 13  games of starting experience at the  college level and he's regarded  potentially as the first overall pick  and that puts only more pressure on him  and you go to a place like Cleveland  where if they stink again this year are  the Haslam's going to continue with the  current front office and coaching staff  and true Biscay could get thrown into a  vortex where even if he otherwise in  another system with another coach with  another owner another city would be  great  you may have no chance in Cleveland so  that's the one thing we have to factor  into this these guys are going to get  assigned to teams that they wouldn't  have maybe chosen if they had their  druthers and you could have a guy who  would have been great somewhere else who  goes to Cleveland er goes to another  city and it all falls apart and it's  really not his fault yeah I'd rather go  to the Arizona Cardinals than I would be  Cleveland Brown I'd rather go late in  the first then early in the first if it  meant the difference of going to  Cleveland or going to Arizona I did look  at the top two picks Cleveland at one  San Francisco at - you've got Kyle  Shanahan and John Lynch with six year  contracts with no offset meaning they're  getting paid the full amount of their  salary for the next six years whether  they're there or not whether they're  working